<Steps>
  <Step subtitle="Write file" title="Save the README to Your Repository">
    Run this command in your terminal to create and populate `README.md`:

    ```bash
    cat << 'EOF' > README.md
    # Git Learning & Version Control Practice

    A practice repository created on Ubuntu to learn basic Git concepts, workflow, and terminal commands.

    ## Topics Covered
    * Initializing a Git repository (`git init`)
    * Checking repository status (`git status`)
    * Tracking and staging changes (`git add`)
    * Committing snapshots locally (`git commit`)
    * Connecting to remote repositories on GitHub (`git remote add`)
    * Pushing local commits to GitHub (`git push`)

    ## Prerequisites
    * Linux/Ubuntu terminal environment
    * Git installed (`git --version`)
    * A GitHub account and Personal Access Token (PAT) for HTTPS authentication

    ## Basic Workflow
    1. **Check status:**
       ```bash
       git status
       ```
    2. **Stage modified/new files:**
       ```bash
       git add .
       ```
    3. **Commit staged changes:**
       ```bash
       git commit -m "Your commit message"
       ```
    4. **Push commits to GitHub:**
       ```bash
       git push -u origin main
       ```
    EOF
    ```

    *Verification:* Run `cat README.md` to ensure the content was written correctly.
  </Step>

  <Step subtitle="Sync with GitHub" title="Stage, Commit, and Push the New README">
    Push your updated `README.md` to GitHub:

    ```bash
    git add README.md
    git commit -m "Update README with Git learning overview"
    git push
    ```

    *Verification:* Refresh `[https://github.com/yunuszoro46-sketch/versionControl](https://github.com/yunuszoro46-sketch/versionControl)` in your browser to view the updated formatted README.
  </Step>
</Steps>

